          "message": {
            "text": "`key` (client-controlled, from `changes`) chooses which entry of `profile` is written. The key is not checked against an allow-list (or a strict pattern): the client chooses which entry is written, for example `Coins` or another player's save. Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
