            "text": "`itemId` (client-controlled) chooses which entry of `profile.Inventory` is written. The key is not checked against an allow-list (or a strict pattern): the client chooses which entry is written, for example `Coins` or another player's save. Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "luauShield/v1": "aab75177c8b3a919"
          },
          "properties": {
            "severity": "high"
          },
          "ruleId": "luau-shield001",
          "ruleIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/TradeService.server.luau",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endColumn": 52,
                  "endLine": 22,
                  "startColumn": 40,
                  "startLine": 22
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`Remotes.ConfirmTrade:InvokeClient()` makes the server wait for an answer from a client, which may never come. Use a RemoteEvent for the request and another for the reply (with a server-side timeout), or at least run the invoke in a detached thread (`task.spawn`) with a timeout and validate the returned values."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "luauShield/v1": "ec4e40038aa684dd"
          },
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "luau-shield006",
