      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield",
          "name": "luau-shield",
          "rules": [
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A value sent by the client reaches leaderstats, currency/stat fields, player data tables, DataStores or MemoryStores without being validated."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A value sent by the client reaches leaderstats, currency/stat fields, player data tables, DataStores or MemoryStores without being validated.\n\n**Why:** Exploiters can fire any remote with any arguments. If the server adds a client-supplied amount to a currency, saves a client-supplied table or lets the client pick the DataStore key, an exploiter can give themselves unlimited currency, corrupt other players' data or poison saves with NaN/huge values.\n\n**Fix:** Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield001.md)",
                "text": "A value sent by the client reaches leaderstats, currency/stat fields, player data tables, DataStores or MemoryStores without being validated.\n\nWhy: Exploiters can fire any remote with any arguments. If the server adds a client-supplied amount to a currency, saves a client-supplied table or lets the client pick the DataStore key, an exploiter can give themselves unlimited currency, corrupt other players' data or poison saves with NaN/huge values.\n\nFix: Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield001.md",
              "id": "luau-shield001",
              "name": "untrusted-economy-write",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Client-controlled value written to currency, stats or saved data"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A value sent by the client is assigned to a property such as Position, CFrame, Health, WalkSpeed, Parent or Text, or passed to PivotTo/TakeDamage/ApplyImpulse/SetAttribute."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A value sent by the client is assigned to a property such as Position, CFrame, Health, WalkSpeed, Parent or Text, or passed to PivotTo/TakeDamage/ApplyImpulse/SetAttribute.\n\n**Why:** The server replicates these properties to everyone. Trusting the client lets exploiters teleport, fly, heal themselves, kill other players, move or delete parts, or display unfiltered text to other players.\n\n**Fix:** Compute the value on the server (from server-side stats, the character's real position, etc.). If it must come from the client, clamp it to a sensible range, check distances against the character, allow-list instances, and filter text with TextService.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield002.md)",
                "text": "A value sent by the client is assigned to a property such as Position, CFrame, Health, WalkSpeed, Parent or Text, or passed to PivotTo/TakeDamage/ApplyImpulse/SetAttribute.\n\nWhy: The server replicates these properties to everyone. Trusting the client lets exploiters teleport, fly, heal themselves, kill other players, move or delete parts, or display unfiltered text to other players.\n\nFix: Compute the value on the server (from server-side stats, the character's real position, etc.). If it must come from the client, clamp it to a sensible range, check distances against the character, allow-list instances, and filter text with TextService."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield002.md",
              "id": "luau-shield002",
              "name": "untrusted-instance-property",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Client-controlled value assigned to a sensitive Instance property"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An Instance received from a remote is modified, destroyed, moved or used as a source of data without verifying that it belongs to the player or is where it should be."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "An Instance received from a remote is modified, destroyed, moved or used as a source of data without verifying that it belongs to the player or is where it should be.\n\n**Why:** A remote can be fired with any Instance the client can see: another player's tool, a door on the other side of the map, a part of someone else's plot. Type checks such as `IsA` only prove what kind of object it is, not that the player is allowed to touch it.\n\n**Fix:** Verify ownership or location before using the Instance: `inst:IsDescendantOf(player.Character)`, compare an `Owner` attribute with `player.UserId`, check the distance to the character, or look it up in a server-side list of allowed instances.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield003.md)",
                "text": "An Instance received from a remote is modified, destroyed, moved or used as a source of data without verifying that it belongs to the player or is where it should be.\n\nWhy: A remote can be fired with any Instance the client can see: another player's tool, a door on the other side of the map, a part of someone else's plot. Type checks such as `IsA` only prove what kind of object it is, not that the player is allowed to touch it.\n\nFix: Verify ownership or location before using the Instance: `inst:IsDescendantOf(player.Character)`, compare an `Owner` attribute with `player.UserId`, check the distance to the character, or look it up in a server-side list of allowed instances."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield003.md",
              "id": "luau-shield003",
              "name": "unverified-client-instance",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Instance sent by the client used without checking ownership or location"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A value sent by the client reaches `loadstring`, `load`, `require` or a dynamic global lookup (`getfenv()[x]`, `_G[x]`)."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A value sent by the client reaches `loadstring`, `load`, `require` or a dynamic global lookup (`getfenv()[x]`, `_G[x]`).\n\n**Why:** This gives the client remote code execution on the server: an exploiter can run arbitrary code with server privileges, require malicious assets by id, delete the game, steal data or ban players.\n\n**Fix:** Never run code or require modules chosen by the client. Dispatch commands through a server-side table of allowed functions (`Commands[name]`) and validate the name against it.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield004.md)",
                "text": "A value sent by the client reaches `loadstring`, `load`, `require` or a dynamic global lookup (`getfenv()[x]`, `_G[x]`).\n\nWhy: This gives the client remote code execution on the server: an exploiter can run arbitrary code with server privileges, require malicious assets by id, delete the game, steal data or ban players.\n\nFix: Never run code or require modules chosen by the client. Dispatch commands through a server-side table of allowed functions (`Commands[name]`) and validate the name against it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield004.md",
              "id": "luau-shield004",
              "name": "untrusted-code-execution",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Client-controlled value reaches loadstring/require"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A value sent by the client is used to build the URL, headers or body of `HttpService:GetAsync/PostAsync/RequestAsync`."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A value sent by the client is used to build the URL, headers or body of `HttpService:GetAsync/PostAsync/RequestAsync`.\n\n**Why:** The client can make your server send requests to arbitrary endpoints or paths, abuse your webhooks and proxies (spam, @everyone pings, Terms of Service violations that get the webhook or game banned) and exhaust the HttpService request budget.\n\n**Fix:** Keep URLs on the server and choose them through an allow-listed key. Encode client values with `HttpService:UrlEncode`, convert ids with `tonumber`, limit the length of text and rate-limit the remote.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield005.md)",
                "text": "A value sent by the client is used to build the URL, headers or body of `HttpService:GetAsync/PostAsync/RequestAsync`.\n\nWhy: The client can make your server send requests to arbitrary endpoints or paths, abuse your webhooks and proxies (spam, @everyone pings, Terms of Service violations that get the webhook or game banned) and exhaust the HttpService request budget.\n\nFix: Keep URLs on the server and choose them through an allow-listed key. Encode client values with `HttpService:UrlEncode`, convert ids with `tonumber`, limit the length of text and rate-limit the remote."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield005.md",
              "id": "luau-shield005",
              "name": "untrusted-http-request",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Client-controlled URL, headers or body in an HttpService request"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The server calls `RemoteFunction:InvokeClient` (or assigns `OnClientInvoke`), so it depends on an answer from an untrusted client."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "The server calls `RemoteFunction:InvokeClient` (or assigns `OnClientInvoke`), so it depends on an answer from an untrusted client.\n\n**Why:** A malicious client can simply never return: the server thread yields forever (pcall does not help), leaking memory and blocking whatever logic waits for the answer. A client that errors or leaves also breaks the call, and every value it returns is client-controlled.\n\n**Fix:** Use a RemoteEvent for the request and another for the reply (with a server-side timeout), or at least run the invoke in a detached thread (`task.spawn`) with a timeout and validate the returned values.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield006.md)",
                "text": "The server calls `RemoteFunction:InvokeClient` (or assigns `OnClientInvoke`), so it depends on an answer from an untrusted client.\n\nWhy: A malicious client can simply never return: the server thread yields forever (pcall does not help), leaking memory and blocking whatever logic waits for the answer. A client that errors or leaves also breaks the call, and every value it returns is client-controlled.\n\nFix: Use a RemoteEvent for the request and another for the reply (with a server-side timeout), or at least run the invoke in a detached thread (`task.spawn`) with a timeout and validate the returned values."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield006.md",
              "id": "luau-shield006",
              "name": "server-invokes-client",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Server waits for a client with RemoteFunction:InvokeClient"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A remote handler calls `*Async` APIs, `Instance.new` or `:Clone()` and has no visible rate limit or debounce."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A remote handler calls `*Async` APIs, `Instance.new` or `:Clone()` and has no visible rate limit or debounce.\n\n**Why:** Exploiters can fire a remote thousands of times per second. Without a limit, each call spends DataStore/HTTP budgets, creates instances or yields, which is enough to lag or crash the server and to exhaust request quotas for everyone.\n\n**Fix:** Add a per-player cooldown (store `os.clock()` per player and return early when called too often), a busy flag while the previous request is running, or a shared rate limiter module.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield007.md)",
                "text": "A remote handler calls `*Async` APIs, `Instance.new` or `:Clone()` and has no visible rate limit or debounce.\n\nWhy: Exploiters can fire a remote thousands of times per second. Without a limit, each call spends DataStore/HTTP budgets, creates instances or yields, which is enough to lag or crash the server and to exhaust request quotas for everyone.\n\nFix: Add a per-player cooldown (store `os.clock()` per player and return early when called too often), a busy flag while the previous request is running, or a shared rate limiter module."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield007.md",
              "id": "luau-shield007",
              "name": "remote-without-rate-limit",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Remote handler does expensive work without a rate limit"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A webhook URL, API key, token or cookie is written in a LocalScript or in a ModuleScript that clients can read."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "A webhook URL, API key, token or cookie is written in a LocalScript or in a ModuleScript that clients can read.\n\n**Why:** Exploiters can decompile every LocalScript and replicated ModuleScript. A leaked webhook can be spammed or deleted, and a leaked API key gives full access to the account or service behind it.\n\n**Fix:** Move the secret to the server (ServerScriptService/ServerStorage), store it with Roblox secrets (`HttpService:GetSecret`) and revoke the leaked credential.\n\n[Documentation](https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield008.md)",
                "text": "A webhook URL, API key, token or cookie is written in a LocalScript or in a ModuleScript that clients can read.\n\nWhy: Exploiters can decompile every LocalScript and replicated ModuleScript. A leaked webhook can be spammed or deleted, and a leaked API key gives full access to the account or service behind it.\n\nFix: Move the secret to the server (ServerScriptService/ServerStorage), store it with Roblox secrets (`HttpService:GetSecret`) and revoke the leaked credential."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield008.md",
              "id": "luau-shield008",
              "name": "client-exposed-secret",
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "roblox",
                  "luau"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Secret hard-coded in code that replicates to clients"
              }
            }
          ],
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.0",
